Lecturer appointments will range from one-quarter- to one-year-time, with the possibility of reappointment, dependent upon performance and departmental needs. Terms and conditions of employment are subject to University of California (UC) policy and any appropriate collective bargaining agreement. The posting will remain open until March 31, 2027 to accommodate department needs. The pool will close on March 31, 2027. When this recruitment closes, if you would like to continue to be considered after that time -- and the pooled position is advertised again -- you will need to submit a new application to the new recruitment. Please note: The use of a lecturer pool does not guarantee that an open position exists at the time you are applying. See the next review date specified in UCRecruit to indicate the next potential upcoming opening. If there is no future review date shown at the time of application submission, your application may possibly not be considered at this time. Department : https://tmp.ucsb.edu/ Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Applicants must possess a minimum of a Bachelor’s Degree at time of application. Preferred qualifications A relevant Master’s and/or Ph.D; At least one year of university-level teaching experience in a relevant field; Executive-level professional experience in relevant areas. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter (Optional) Statement of Teaching -   The \"Statement of Teaching\" is meant to provide insight into past teaching experiences, teaching methods, teaching in various settings (in person vs. on-line), and to get a general idea about your teaching background. Reference requirements 3-5 required (contact information only) Candidates who are considered finalists may have their references contacted. Apply link: https://recruit.ap.ucsb.edu/JPF03095 Help contact: nicoleleick@ucsb.edu About UC Santa Barbara As a condition 